{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1023","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Pair of Toys"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tanechka is shopping in the toy shop. There are exactly $$$n$$$ toys in the shop for sale, the cost of the $$$i$$$-th toy is $$$i$$$ burles. She wants to choose two toys in such a way that their total cost is $$$k$$$ burles. How many ways to do that does she have?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each toy appears in the shop exactly once. Pairs $$$(a, b)$$$ and $$$(b, a)$$$ are considered equal. Pairs $$$(a, b)$$$, where $$$a=b$$$, are not allowed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers $$$n$$$, $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, k \\le 10^{14}$$$) — the number of toys and the expected total cost of the pair of toys."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the number of ways to choose the pair of toys satisfying the condition above. Print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if Tanechka can choose no pair of toys in such a way that their total cost is $$$k$$$ burles."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 15\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7 20\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1000000000000 1000000000001\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"500000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example Tanechka can choose the pair of toys ($$$1, 4$$$) or the pair of toys ($$$2, 3$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example Tanechka can choose only the pair of toys ($$$7, 8$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example choosing any pair of toys will lead to the total cost less than $$$20$$$. So the answer is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth example she can choose the following pairs: $$$(1, 1000000000000)$$$, $$$(2, 999999999999)$$$, $$$(3, 999999999998)$$$, ..., $$$(500000000000, 500000000001)$$$. The number of such pairs is exactly $$$500000000000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1023B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1023/problem/B"}